SUMMARY:Scenic AVL #8: Beaver Lake to Reynolds Mountain
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nThis route goes up Reynolds Mounta
 in and rambles along the ridge line. We do not go around Beaver Lake becau
 se of their dog rules.\n\n**Rating:** Strenuous (climb up Reynolds is stee
 p)\n**Distance:** 6 miles\n**Elevation Gain:** 1000 ft\n**Surface:** Road\
 n**Sun Exposure: 90%. There is almost no shade on this hike**\n**Pace:** 3
 .2 mph\, best effort on push up Reynolds\n**Features:** Lake views\, mount
 ain views\n**Bears:** Not likely\n**Dogs:** On leash\n**Gear:** in winter\
 , please bring a headlamp. In summer\, this hike is very hot and exposed\,
  so bring water and/or a hat. No flip-flops.\n\n**Parking is limited** at 
 the triangle\, but there is overflow parking available at Beaver Lake Bird
  Sanctuary. If you park at Beaver Lake Bird Sanctuary\, CALL the hike lead
 er at 828-290-0886 and let me know. Please walk to the Triangle to join th
 e group. Alternatively\, arrange a car pool from Ingles on Merrimon with o
 thers in the group by making a note in the comments below.\n\n**Route:** [
 Reynold's Mountain Winter Route](https://www.alltrails.com/explore/map/rey
 nolds-mountain-winter-version-43fa7f5?u=i&sh=ifwm3x)\n\n**Scenic Asheville
  Series:** There are [9 hikes in the series](https://docs.google.com/docum
 ent/d/11ewlUM9OV8I4npc1cNNsSYOnXI0QPw2isAleXdFzEbI/edit?usp=sharing)\; hik
 e them all and receive an[ attractive badge](https://docs.google.com/drawi
 ngs/d/1goXUXfzUBqhB4_UeCxodlk4ZPeCCgqZrWK2EUJvk_vI/edit?usp=sharing) for y
 our backpack. Check your progress **[HERE](https://docs.google.com/spreads
 heets/d/1XUm-X1_OhxKIi8JU5rhjsW37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?gid=0#gid=0).**\
 nSpecial bonus for badge holders: You can always come on a hike\, even if 
 you are on the wait list. See our [highlights here](https://docs.google.co
 m/presentation/d/18cFp2Uhw8XthOFXxekBpt2LGP6ww-V7kmXQExI7Y0h0/)!\n\n**Wait
  List:** If someone is waiting on a particular hike for their badge\, they
  may be moved to Going ahead of other people. If I notice you need one mor
 e hike for your badge\, I may auto-add you to the hike.\n\n**Guests:** If 
 you bring a guest\, please add them as a plus one on the app so it will ad
 d them to the count of attendees. Make sure your guest knows the distance 
 and elevation gain\, and carries appropriate gear (water\, headlamp in win
 ter). Also\, if someone comes as a guest\, it won't count toward a badge\,
  because I won't have record of their name (unless you text it to me or ot
 herwise make special effort so that I know they attended).\n\n**RSVP and O
 n-Time Start:**\n\n*If you decide you cannot come\, please change your RSV
 P\n- If you must cancel\, please change your status to "Not Going" as soon
  as possible so wait-listers can have sufficient notice.\n*There are gener
 ally 1 or 2 no-shows on my hikes\, so we don't wait for people to arrive. 
 If you are late\, you'll be left behind. In some hikes\, there are "if lat
 e" instructions to intercept us.\n- Notes and comments are genuinely appre
 ciated.\n\n**Disclaimer and Release of Liability:**\nThis activity involve
 s hiking on city streets that may have traffic. Participants are responsib
 le for their safety on streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a
  volunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is 
 only to organize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event yo
 u acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of
  injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and as
 sociated with this event. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to 
 the Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/te
 rms)
